# Latin coordinating and subordinating conjunctions (closed class).
# Written from own knowledge (AUTHORING.md §1); format: Heinrich docs/LEXICON_FORMAT_LA.md §7.
-que cconj
-ve cconj
antequam sconj
ast cconj style=poetic|archaic
at cconj
atque|ac cconj
atquī|atquīn cconj conf=80 note=length of the i?
attamen cconj
aut cconj
autem cconj
ceu sconj
cum|quom[archaic]|quum[medieval] sconj
dōnec sconj
dum sconj
dummodo sconj
enim cconj
ergō cconj
et cconj
etenim cconj
etiamsī sconj
etsī sconj
igitur cconj
itaque cconj
nam cconj
namque cconj
nē sconj
nec|neque cconj
nēve|neu cconj conf=85 note=length of the e?
nisi|nī sconj
postquam sconj
priusquam sconj
quamquam sconj
quamvīs sconj
quandō sconj
quasi sconj
quia sconj
quīn sconj
quō sconj
quoad sconj
quod sconj
quōminus sconj
quoniam sconj
sed cconj
sī sconj
sīcut|sīcutī sconj
simulac|simulatque sconj
sīn sconj
sīve|seu cconj
tametsī sconj
tamquam sconj
ubi sconj
ut|utī sconj
vel cconj
velut|velutī sconj
vērō cconj
vērum cconj
